The unfamiliar-reader review is written to `docs/content-analysis/pipeline-logs/2026-10-11_18-12-25-028_Doja-Cat/review-unfamiliar.json`. It passes `reviewSchema`, both hashes match the frozen draft and evidence, and every finding and protected passage is an exact substring of the draft. Nothing else was modified and nothing was published.

The review has nine findings (four major, five minor) and five protected passages. That is one over the eight-finding target, because two are date errors on the page's own facts.

**Major**
- **unfamiliar-01:** The 60-word answer and FAQ 1 say she "erupts later, over a stage name", but the body shows no eruption over the name. She tried to change it, was talked out of it, and kept it.
- **unfamiliar-02:** "The sequence repeats with different casts" is not shown by the Threads and Auckland bullets, which have no going-along step and no repair. Only three of the six blowups narrated show a preceding yes, so the title's "Every Blowup" and FAQ 3 overclaim.
- **unfamiliar-03:** The body never says plainly who she is or how big the career was. "Say So" is absent, "Hot Pink" appears only inside a lowercase tweet, and "Scarlet" is used before it is introduced.
- **unfamiliar-04:** Her father's March 2026 denial is presented as his answer to an Elle UK interview published in May 2026. The same reversed order is in FAQ 6.

**Minor**
- **unfamiliar-05:** "Before anyone was angry at her" (about 2021 statements) contradicts the May 2020 controversy in the page's own FAQ.
- **unfamiliar-06:** Interviewers, witnesses and the ashram arrive without a gloss, and "I can be strategic" has no claim passage.
- **unfamiliar-07:** The Type 7 section comes after the Nine-versus-Six contest is settled, so momentum drops; the shaved-head example gives her quote but not what it shows.
- **unfamiliar-08:** The key caveat is written in shorthand ("the smoothing"), and Type 6 is not described until the eighth section.
- **unfamiliar-09:** "That is her own explanation of this cycle" asserts a link between her October 2025 remark and her March 2026 statement that the page does not show her making.

Risk flags are carried from research unchanged: sensitive allegations, contested typing and major thesis change are true; historical source uncertainty is false.

Two things to know about how I worked:
- **Similarity:** the one tripped pair shares only "keep the peace". I opened the Austin Abrams, Victoria Justice and Nate Bargatze drafts to compare the matched passages in context and found ordinary Type 9 vocabulary, so there is no reuse finding.
- **Sources:** I did not reopen any; dates and context come from the supplied evidence record, and the review says so.
